{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxBDEtiVTeesybBC7kVb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the one thing I can actually show was broken: the test run. `tox.ini` told pytest to collect from a `tests/` folder that doesn't exist, so the command errored out (\"no tests ran\") before reaching any doctest. That breaks `tox` and every job in the GitHub Actions tests workflow.\n\nI removed `{tox_root}/tests` from the command in `tox.ini`, so it now runs only the doctests. Run locally, all 80 pass. I didn't run tox itself, because network access is blocked here and it needs to install packages.\n\nThis change also means there's no real test suite any more, only doctests. If the `tests/` folder was deleted by accident, restoring it is the better fix, and I'll undo this edit once it's back.\n\nIf this wasn't the problem you meant, the code itself looks fine to me. All 8 modules import, the doctests pass, and about 90 extra checks I wrote match upstream boltons behavior. Two smaller loose ends:\n- **Docs:** `docs/` still has pages for about 20 modules that aren't in the repo, so a docs or ReadTheDocs build will fail on those pages. I can trim them.\n- **Packaging:** `pyproject.toml` still lists `tests/` and `doc/` in the sdist includes. `doc/` looks like a typo for `docs/`.\n\nIf something else is failing, paste the command and its output and I'll go straight at it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":57243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":939},"output_tokens":459,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fbe6c21-c005-46c7-8bb3-561d25b7c291","uuid":"3e7761db-71ee-4414-ab12-cc1813cd8373","t